 7.3 Logout That Clears Cart

jsx
// SettingsScreen.js
const { logout } = useContext(AuthContext);
const { clearCart } = useCart();

const confirmLogout = () => {
  Alert.alert('Log out', 'Are you sure?', [
    { text: 'Cancel', style: 'cancel' },
    {
      text: 'Log out',
      style: 'destructive',
      onPress: () => {
        clearCart?.();   // wipe cart first
        logout?.();      // then clear token
      },
    },
  ]);
};




 8. Bugs Fixed Along the Way (Reference)

|  | Bug | Root cause | Fix |
||--||--|
| 1 | `GO_BACK` warning on Products | Registered as sibling tab, not stack child | Created `HomeStack`, nested inside Home tab |
| 2 | No back button on stack screens | `screenOptions.headerLeft` shadowed per-screen override | Removed global `headerLeft`, kept it only on `HomeMain` |
| 3 | `CustomButton` icon ignored | Import `Icon` shadowed by prop `Icon` | Renamed import → `Ionicons`, prop → `icon` |
| 4 | Chip text invisible | `colors.white` undefined → `CustomText` default kicked in | Add `white: 'FFFFFF'` alias to theme |
| 5 | Chips resize with content | `paddingVertical` instead of fixed `height` | `height: 36` + `borderRadius: 18` |
| 6 | Cart math produced NaN | Prices stored as `'₹1,999'` strings | Store prices as numbers, format in view with `toLocaleString('en-IN')` |



 9. Interview Talking Points

When demonstrating this project, mention these decisions:

1. Conditional root navigator — auth state drives the entire app's navigation tree. No manual redirects after login/logout.
2. Nested navigators — Stack inside Tab inside Drawer. Each layer has one job. Back navigation "just works" because the flow screens live in a stack.
3. Two focused contexts — `AuthContext` and `CartContext` are separate. Neither is a "god context." Each has a single responsibility.
4. Custom hooks around context — `useCart()` throws a clear error if the provider is missing. Better DX than silent failures.
5. Reusable UI primitives with props — `CustomText`, `CustomButton`, `SettingsRow` all take semantic props, not raw style objects. Screens stay declarative.
6. Theme as single source of truth — no hardcoded colors, sizes, or spacing in screens. Changing `colors.primary` instantly re-skins the app.
7. Left-aligned dividers in menus — margin-left matches `icon width + gap` so the divider aligns with the label, not the icon. Tiny detail that signals polish.
8. Fixed-height chips with pill radius — `borderRadius = height / 2` creates perfect pills regardless of label length.
9. Derived state via `useMemo` — `subtotal`, `savings`, `totalItems` are computed, never stored. Impossible for them to drift out of sync with `items`.
10. Confirmation before destructive actions — logout and delete account both go through `Alert.alert`. Prevents accidental data loss.



